docs {
  ## Submit Dynamic Survey

  Submits answers for the dynamic, project-scoped survey system.

  ### Fields
  | Field | Required | Description |
  |---|---|---|
  | projectId | Yes | Which project's question set these answers belong to |
  | institutionId | No | FK to institution, if the school is matched to one |
  | schoolName | No | Fallback display name if not matched to an institution |
  | taskId | No | FK to the task_list row this survey was assigned through (Task Activity > Implementation > Survey). When present, that task is auto-marked Completed once the submission is saved — no separate status-update call needed. |
  | answers | Yes | JSON array — see format below |
  | `<q_id>` file fields | No | For each `q_type: 'photo'` question being answered, attach a file field named after that question's `q_id` (e.g. `PHOTO_FRONT`). Attach it more than once (same field name, up to 5 times) to upload multiple photos for that one question — no `answers` entry is needed for photo questions at all, the file(s) alone are enough |

  ### `answers` JSON format
  ```json
  [
    { "questionId": 122, "value": "Test School" },
    { "questionId": 154, "value": "true", "remarks": "Paved road, 2km" },
    { "questionId": 157, "value": "Clear" },
    { "questionId": 191, "value": "" }
  ]
  ```
  - `questionId` — the `question_id` from `GET /survey/questions`
  - `repeatIndex` (optional, default 1) — which instance this answer belongs
    to, for `repeat_group` questions (1st classroom vs 2nd classroom, etc.)
  - `value` — the answer. Not used for `q_type: 'photo'` questions — those
    are driven entirely by the attached file field(s), see above
  - `remarks` (optional) — free-text note alongside this specific answer. For
    a `q_type: 'photo'` question, include one entry with just `questionId`
    and `remarks` (no `value` needed) to attach a remark to all of that
    question's photos

  ### Multiple photos per question (up to 5)
  Attach the same field, named after the question's `q_id`, multiple times in
  the multipart body — each attachment becomes its own image, in the order
  attached. A 6th+ file for the same question is accepted by the upload but
  discarded and not saved to any answer. Every image is returned in the
  response as its own entry in `answers`, sharing the same `q_id`/`question`
  but with an increasing `repeat_index` (1st photo, 2nd photo, ...).

  Answers referencing a `questionId` that doesn't belong to the given
  `projectId` are silently skipped, not errored.

  ### Response
  Full submission record with every saved answer, each including its
  question's `q_id`/`section`/`question`/`q_type` for easy display without a
  second lookup.
}

tests {
  test("Status 201", function() { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); });
  test("success true", function() { expect(res.getBody().success).to.equal(true); });
  test("has submission_id", function() { expect(res.getBody().data).to.have.property("submission_id"); });
  test("has answers", function() { expect(res.getBody().data.answers).to.be.an("array"); });
}
